---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | BarkLens"
  description="The BarkLens privacy commitments for records, account information, export, and deletion."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="policy-page">
    <header class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Your records are not our business model.</h1>
      <p>The plain-English version first. Counsel-approved policy language will replace the draft below before launch.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="policy-page__promises container">
      <article><h2>We read what you add, nothing else.</h2><p>BarkLens processes only the records and information you choose to add.</p></article>
      <article><h2>You approve what stays.</h2><p>Each record is shown to you first. Approve it and it joins your dog’s chart.</p></article>
      <article><h2>Never sold.</h2><p>No data brokers and no advertising business built from your dog’s records.</p></article>
      <article><h2>Leave with everything.</h2><p>Export your dog’s records. Account-deletion details will match the final policy and product.</p></article>
    </section>
    <section class="policy-page__draft container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Draft coverage</p>
      <h2>The final policy will explain:</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Account information, records, questions, and technical information BarkLens collects.</li>
        <li>How uploaded records and photographs are processed and retained.</li>
        <li>Service providers involved in storage, AI processing, analytics, and email.</li>
        <li>Access, export, correction, account closure, and deletion.</li>
        <li>Care Team sharing and what invited people can see.</li>
        <li>Security practices, retention periods, and contact information.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@barklens.com">hello@barklens.com</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy-page > header { padding-block: var(--space-24) var(--space-12); }
  .policy-page h1 { max-width: 15ch; margin-top: var(--space-5); font-size: var(--text-2xl); }
  .policy-page header > p:last-child { max-width: 52ch; margin-top: var(--space-6); color: var(--color-copy-muted); }
  .policy-page__promises { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-5); }
  .policy-page__promises article { padding: var(--space-8); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--color-forest-900); color: var(--color-copy-inverse); }
  .policy-page__promises h2 { color: var(--color-mint-400); font-size: var(--text-lg); }
  .policy-page__promises p { margin-top: var(--space-3); color: #d8cfc0; }
  .policy-page__draft { max-width: var(--content-narrow); padding-block: var(--space-20); }
  .policy-page__draft h2 { margin-top: var(--space-5); font-size: var(--text-xl); }
  .policy-page__draft ul { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); margin-top: var(--space-6); padding-left: var(--space-6); color: var(--color-copy-muted); }
  .policy-page__draft > p:last-child { margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .policy-page__draft a { color: var(--color-green-600); font-weight: 700; }
  @media (max-width: 47.99rem) { .policy-page__promises { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
